  "baseRefOid": "4625afd492b6cf43e3b499d1425d2453d490009d",
  "body": "The current-input SSSOM generation reported 41 native invariant failures despite the maintained canonical mapping passing QC. This evidence companion to [Claw PR #683](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/culturebotai-claw/pull/683) records their generator-side causes and verifies the repaired candidate: 2,980 rows, zero native invariant rejects.\n\n- Rule B5: preserve the 14 curated registry identities and remove 14 competing generated identities, resolving 28 rejected entries.\n- Rule K: remove inherited target aliases from non-exact mappings, resolving all 11 collisions while retaining permitted subject-owned synonyms.\n- Rule G: derive both header dates from the newest valid row date, resolving both mismatches. Independent review also found a Unicode-date guard defect; Claw issue #682 was filed before its fix and final-head re-review passed.\n\nThe original structured review is preserved byte-for-byte. Its successor retains the three finding keys, prior-occurrence links and all 41 diagnostic selectors. The report contains exact input revisions and hashes, per-row dispositions, mutation-test evidence, validator logs, scientific hold records and independent code-review reports. Final generator head `8f837d505b948a25965b0b2a001a4c7691c840fc` produces a byte-identical replay of the repaired candidate.\n\nValidation: MIM `just qc` passes, including `qc-sssom`, roundtrip and flat coverage. The candidate separately passes native invariants, SSSOM schema/prefix/CURIE checks, configured ID-label validation and drift reconciliation. Native structured-review validation and the 978-bundle check pass. The Claw fix passes 66 focused tests and its full CI-style suite (6,012 passed, 377 skipped, 87.83% coverage); the safety-module coverage gate passes at 76%.\n\nIndependent adversarial review of evidence head `bb65a909e5f56b2400f64a2e363d9ad60a2996a9` found no new defects. It independently checked committed bytes, hashes, all 41 dispositions, preserved scientific holds and the 978-bundle native review gate.\n\nAll changes here are review/report evidence. The canonical mapping, ingredient YAML, aggregate collections, unified mapping, pinned scientific review and cycle artifacts remain unchanged. The candidate is diagnostic and is not promoted: existing scientific holds, ontology-adapter skips and best-effort B4 coverage limits remain documented. PR #914 and the Intel Cycle 12 work are outside this change.\n\nDefect issues: [Claw #679](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/culturebotai-claw/issues/679), [#680](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/culturebotai-claw/issues/680), [#681](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/culturebotai-claw/issues/681), [#682](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/culturebotai-claw/issues/682).\n\nThis PR is draft to prevent scheduled merge-queue admission. Merge remains a user decision.\n",
